{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Hass1967-AR3-MgF2-ZrO2-CeF3-glass",
  "Source": "G. Hass and E. Ritter, \"Optical film materials and their applications,\" J. Vac. Sci. Technol. 4, 71-79 (1967). doi:10.1116/1.1492525 - Fig. 6 and caption, p. 74 ('CeF3 + ZrO2 + MgF2 on crown glass. Layers lambda/4 - lambda/2 - lambda/4 thick at lambda = 550 mu'); indices from Fig. 5 chart, p. 74",
  "Notes": "Triple-layer visible antireflection coating on crown glass (quarter - half - quarter design)\nSpecification: Broadband visible AR on crown glass, single surface.\nReported: Fig. 6 (measured, single-surface reflectance, normal incidence assumed): R about 2.3 % at 400 nm, falling to a minimum of about 0.1 % near 450-470 nm, a broad hump of about 0.3 % around 550-600 nm, about 0.0 % near 700-750 nm, rising to about 0.3 % at 800 nm and 1.0 % at 850 nm (end of curve). Uncoated glass reference line at about 4.1-4.2 %. All values read from the plot (no table).\nNotes: The caption lists the materials from the glass outward (CeF3 + ZrO2 + MgF2) together with thicknesses lambda/4 - lambda/2 - lambda/4; since both ends are quarter waves the order of thicknesses is the same either way. The usual construction (and the only one that makes sense for AR) has CeF3 next to the glass and MgF2 outermost, so the list is reversed here: layer 1 = MgF2 (air side). Indices are the visible values printed in Fig. 5 (CeF3 1.63, ZrO2 2.1, MgF2 1.38, labelled near 0.55 um); taken as non-dispersive. Crown glass index not given; n = 1.52 assumed (the uncoated-glass line at about 4.15 % corresponds to n of about 1.515). Reflectance is from the coated front surface only (Fig. 6 axis: 'percent reflectance (single surface)'). Normal incidence assumed (not stated).\nLayers from Fig. 6 and caption, p. 74 ('CeF3 + ZrO2 + MgF2 on crown glass. Layers lambda/4 - lambda/2 - lambda/4 thick at lambda = 550 mu'); indices from Fig. 5 chart, p. 74; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), compare with the paper: ours R 4.62 % at 400, 0.0908 % at 460, 0.156 % at 575, 0.467 % at 725, 3.57 % at 850 nm; paper measured (Fig. 6): ~2.3 %, ~0.1 %, ~0.3 %, ~0 %, ~1.0 %.",
